# Local-only data. Two kinds, both kept out of a public repo on purpose:
#
# 1. Vendor-copyrighted material. Adobe's DCP camera profiles (and anything
#    derived from them, like the parsed dcp_standard.json) are Adobe's
#    copyrighted data extracted from the DNG Converter for local research.
#    Redistributing them would be infringement - the parser and fit scripts
#    are ours, the tables are not. Same rule for anything of Nikon's.
# 2. Personal corpus derivatives: pair dumps, sample tensors and per-shot
#    EXIF/XMP features carry shoot names and metadata from private photos.
profiles
*.dcp
dcp_standard.json
pairs2
*.npz
features2.json
images2.json
maker_features.json
makernotes_all.json
faces.jsonl
__pycache__/
